3. STRATEGIC DDD ARCHITECTURE

Identify the complete business domain landscape.

Classify domains into:

Core Domains

Business capabilities that provide the primary competitive and operational value.

Supporting Domains

Business capabilities necessary to operate GCMS but not the central differentiator.

Generic Domains

Common capabilities that can be implemented using standard reusable solutions.

Do not classify all banking functionality as a core domain.

Provide a detailed domain classification matrix.

Domain	Subdomain	Classification	Business Value	Business Owner
Cash Management	Cash Position	Core	Global cash visibility	Treasury
Cash Management	Cash Realignment	Core	Cash optimization	Treasury
Liquidity Management	Liquidity Optimization	Core	Liquidity efficiency	Treasury
Payment Management	Payment Matching	Core	Transaction reconciliation	Payments
Cash Forecasting	Cash Projection	Core	Liquidity planning	Treasury
Accounting	General Ledger	Core/Supporting	Financial integrity	Finance
Entity Management	Legal Entity Hierarchy	Supporting	Organizational structure	Finance
Bank Connectivity	Statement Integration	Supporting	Banking data ingestion	Operations
Security	Identity Management	Generic	Access control	IT
Reporting	Report Generation	Supporting	Financial visibility	Finance

Review and adjust these classifications according to the business context.

