5. DDD BOUNDED CONTEXT DESIGN

For every bounded context, create a detailed specification.

Each specification must contain:

1. Bounded Context Name
2. Business Domain
3. Subdomain
4. Business Purpose
5. Business Scope
6. Functional Responsibilities
7. Explicitly Excluded Responsibilities
8. Business Owner
9. Domain Experts
10. Primary Actors
11. Ubiquitous Language
12. Aggregate Roots
13. Entities
14. Value Objects
15. Domain Services
16. Domain Events
17. Commands
18. Queries
19. Invariants
20. Business Rules
21. State Transitions
22. Database Ownership
23. API Responsibilities
24. Integration Dependencies
25. Upstream Contexts
26. Downstream Contexts
27. Security Requirements
28. Audit Requirements
29. Transaction Boundaries
30. Failure Handling

Do not create overlapping bounded contexts with the same authoritative data ownership.

